        "orario": "21:35",
        "timestamp": 1776800119,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Significant 'overlap' between auto industry and arms manufacturing, expert says Europe Issued on: 21/04/2026 - 21:35 The European automobile industry is pivoting from car production to manufacturing combat drones and defense systems as the continent seeks to rearm in the face of Russia's continued threats. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Rico Luman, Senior Economist for Transport and Logistics at ING Bank, explains that there is an extensive overlap in expertise between auto and weapons engineering that can be successfully exploited to boost Europe's defense industry. 'Mood shifting' in Europe: Public opinion and governments 'turning against Israel' 21/04/2026 Middle East Jet fuel prices flying sky high 21/04/2026 Europe Full suspension of trade relations with Israel requires EU unanimity 21/04/2026 Europe EU pushes to limit carry-on bag fees 21/04/2026 Europe EU hosts Palestinian peace conference 21/04/2026 Middle East EU mulls ending trade agreement with Israel over human rights concerns 21/04/2026 Europe 'Unprecedented since 1999': Radev secures absolute majority with reformist and eurosceptic coalition 20/04/2026 Europe Bulgaria's pro-Russian former president takes strong lead 20/04/2026 Europe Ukrainian best-selling author, Andrey Kurkov speaks to France 24 19/04/2026 Europe"
